     "explanation": "Lencioni's causal sequence describes a general pattern in how teams coordinate, which is why it transfers across contexts. What doesn't transfer automatically is the mechanism — hallway trust-building and easy-to-read body language don't exist on a video call or across functional reporting lines, so those need to be deliberately rebuilt rather than assumed.",
